    "result_text": "The build succeeds \u2014 the only test in the suite (`AcceptanceTest`) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the per-city owner capacity rule: creating an owner is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nChanges, following the existing duplicate-telephone / duplicate-household conventions:\n\n1. **`CityOwnerLimitException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` signaling the business-rule conflict, mirroring the existing `DuplicateTelephoneException` / `DuplicateHouseholdException`.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 added `assertCityCapacity(owner)`, invoked in `saveOwner` for new owners only (so updates aren't affected). It reuses the existing `countOwnersInCity` helper and a `CITY_OWNER_LIMIT = 50` constant, throwing when the city is already at capacity.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `CityOwnerLimitException` that maps it to HTTP 409, consistent with the other conflict handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity`) fills a fresh city to 50 owners and confirms the 51st is rejected with 409 \u2014 green.",
