        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing structure:\n\n- `assertCityCapacity` follows the established `assertTelephoneUnique` / `assertHouseholdAllowed` helper convention, and is invoked from the same `saveOwner` orchestration in the natural `owner.isNew()` block.\n- It reuses the existing `countOwnersInCity` helper rather than duplicating the repository-stream logic \u2014 the right unit already existed and is being leveraged.\n- `CityOwnerLimitException` is a dedicated business-rule exception living in the `service` package alongside the existing `DuplicateHouseholdException` / `DuplicateTelephoneException`, matching the codebase's pattern.\n- The `ExceptionControllerAdvice` handler is a faithful copy of the sibling handlers (same `detailBuild` call, logging, `ResponseEntity.status(...).body(detail)` shape), so a maintainer would find it immediately familiar.\n\nThe one debatable point \u2014 declaring `CITY_OWNER_LIMIT` mid-class rather than in a fields section at the top \u2014 is defensible here: the class has no existing constants section (only injected repositories), and the constant is colocated with its sole consumer. Not worth a change request."
